<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 20 September, from 1058 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-i-of-hungary" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andrew-i-of-hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1058 CE <span class="tih-ago">968 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Agnes of Poitou and Andrew I of Hungary negotiate their border</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Agnes of Poitou, regent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> for her son Henry IV, met King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-i-of-hungary">Andrew I of Hungary</a> to negotiate the border in the area of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a>. It remained the western frontier of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> until the 16th century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-i-of-hungary">Andrew I of Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1066">1066 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Harald Hardrada and Tostig defeat Edwin and Morcar at Fulford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a>, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, and his English ally Tostig Godwinson defeated the northern earls Edwin and Morcar at Fulford, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, in his bid for the English throne. Harald and Tostig were both killed at Stamford Bridge that year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1187">1187 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">839 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Saladin begins the siege of Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s army arrived before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, held by the crusaders for 88 years. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balian-of-ibelin">Balian of Ibelin</a> surrendered the city twelve days later, and most inhabitants were allowed to ransom themselves.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1217">1217 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">809 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prince Louis of France renounces his claim to the English throne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Prince Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, proclaimed King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> by rebel barons, ratified the Treaty of Lambeth after defeats at Lincoln, Dover and Sandwich, ending the First Barons' War. He was paid 10,000 marks and pledged never to invade England again.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-viii-of-france">Louis VIII of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1260">1260 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">766 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Prussian Uprising against the Teutonic Knights begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Encouraged by the defeat of the Livonian Order and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> at Durbe, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-prussians">Old Prussians</a> rose against the Teutonic Order, each clan choosing its own leader, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herkus-monte">Herkus Monte</a> of the Natangians. The knights crushed the revolt by 1274.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-prussians">Old Prussians</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1378">1378 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">648 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert of Geneva is elected Clement VII, beginning the Western Schism</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cardinals who opposed Pope Urban VI elected Robert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> as Clement VII, the first antipope to reside in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a>. Rival popes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and Avignon, and from 1409 a third line from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>, claimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> until 1417.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1519">1519 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">507 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Magellan sets sail to find a western route to the Spice Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan</a> left Sanlúcar de Barrameda with five ships and about 270 men. He was killed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, but one ship returned in 1522, completing the first voyage round the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italian troops breach the walls of Rome at Porta Pia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After French troops left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, Italian forces broke through the walls and took the city. The Papal States ended, and Rome became the capital of united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> the following year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Billie Jean King beats Bobby Riggs in the 'Battle of the Sexes'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Before some 30,000 spectators in Houston and a huge TV audience, Billie Jean King beat former champion Bobby Riggs in straight sets. The match became a landmark for women's sport.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 20 September <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christian-the-younger-of-brunswick"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christian-the-younger-of-brunswick.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christian the Younger of Brunswick</span><span class="tp">1599–1626</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/chulalongkorn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/chulalongkorn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Chulalongkorn</span><span class="tp">1853–1910</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ananda-mahidol"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ananda-mahidol.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ananda Mahidol</span><span class="tp">1925–1946</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 20 September <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-of-chernigov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mikhail-of-chernigov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mikhail of Chernigov</span><span class="tp">c. 1185–1246</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-elector-of-brandenburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick I, Elector of Brandenburg</span><span class="tp">1371–1440</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/veit-stoss"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/veit-stoss.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Veit Stoss</span><span class="tp">c. 1447–1533</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fletcher-christian"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fletcher-christian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fletcher Christian</span><span class="tp">1764–1793</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-gaspar-rodriguez-de-francia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-gaspar-rodriguez-de-francia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Gaspar Rodríguez de Francia</span><span class="tp">1766–1840</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/karlis-ulmanis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/karlis-ulmanis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kārlis Ulmanis</span><span class="tp">1877–1942</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-sibelius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-sibelius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean Sibelius</span><span class="tp">1865–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-seferis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-seferis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Seferis</span><span class="tp">1900–1971</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludvik-svoboda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludvik-svoboda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludvík Svoboda</span><span class="tp">1895–1979</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/burhanuddin-rabbani"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/burhanuddin-rabbani.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Burhanuddin Rabbani</span><span class="tp">1940–2011</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
